Where 𝐹 is the GHG emission flux in mg m−2 h−1; ρ is the gas density in its standard state; h is the height of the static box (m); 
dcdt
 is the rate of change of GHG concentrations in the static box (a linear fit was used, with R2 detecting the goodness of fit), and T is the temperature of the gas chamber during the sampling period (°C).
